# ==============================================================================
# ResQNet — Production Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Client-side Environment Variables (Required for Vite frontend build & runtime)
# Provide these in your production hosting provider's dashboard (Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare, etc.)
# or in your local .env file.
#
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-or-publishable-key

# ==============================================================================
# CRITICAL SECURITY POLICIES:
# ==============================================================================
# 1. NEVER add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to frontend environment variables or .env.
#    The service-role key bypasses Row-Level Security (RLS) and must never be exposed.
#
# 2. NEVER add GEMINI_API_KEY to frontend environment variables or .env.
#    All Gemini AI processing is handled securely server-side via the deployed
#    Supabase Edge Function (`analyze-emergency`).
#    Set the secret in Supabase CLI / Dashboard:
#      supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY="your-google-gemini-api-key" --project-ref your-project-ref
#
# ==============================================================================
# SUPABASE AUTH CONFIGURATION IN DASHBOARD:
# ==============================================================================
# Under Authentication -> URL Configuration:
# - Site URL: https://your-production-domain.com
# - Redirect URLs:
#   - https://your-production-domain.com/**
#   - http://localhost:5173/** (for local testing)
# ==============================================================================
